The paper confirms the native task and its fault line: unrestricted dominating-set TAR reachability is PSPACE-complete, while trees/interval graphs/cographs are linear-time and the paper’s high-threshold constructions are polynomial. I’m therefore not making a Track A claim. I’m testing a Track B design: exact shortest TAR sequences with a hidden precedence chain, where generic search is mechanical but the chain gives a compact route; the verifier will replay the native token moves exactly.
