+The graph has {len(inst['edges'])} edges, listed once each as two endpoints:
+{edge_lines}
+
+Give exactly {inst['required_moves']} moves.  This is the symmetric-difference lower
+bound, so it is a shortest sequence: every target-only vertex must be added once,
+every source-only vertex must be removed once, and no other vertex may be moved.
+Encode adding vertex v by the positive integer v and removing it by -v.  Zero is
+never a move.  The JSON list must alternate an addition and a removal, beginning
+with an addition; vertex labels are 1-based and the order of moves matters.
+
+Give your final answer inside <answer></answer> tags, as one JSON list of signed integers.
+Format-only example (not asserted to be legal): <answer>{json.dumps(format_example, separators=(',', ':'))}</answer>
+Output nothing else inside the tags."""
